# Notebooks

`city_information_modeler/notebooks/` is for local testing. A cell imports from `core` or
`app` and calls it. Geometry, source parsing, physics and file I/O belong in `core/` first;
if a cell grows past a call and a look at the result, move it.

Core functions take a GeoDataFrame or GeoJSON and return the same kind of object, so a
notebook can run them without a database or a pipeline.

Call a core method directly to run the whole job in this process. Use
`parallel.Runner` when you want it split across workers; both give the same answer.
